451		complete only modulo the three low-degree-test obligations. Since the
452		expanded state $\ket{\hat\psi}$ of Definition~\ref{def:expanded-state} is
453		exactly $\ket{\psi}$ with the halves of $M$ pairs
454		$\ket{\mathrm{EPR}_q}$ appended locally in registers
455		$\mathrm{A}'\mathrm{A}''$ and $\mathrm{B}'\mathrm{B}''$, we have
456		$\phi_{\mathrm{A}} \ot \phi_{\mathrm{B}} \ket{\psi}
457		= V_{\mathrm{A}} \ot V_{\mathrm{B}} \ket{\hat\psi}$.
458		Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-unitary} therefore yields a state $\ket{\mathrm{aux}}$
459		on registers $\mathrm{A}\mathrm{A}'\mathrm{B}\mathrm{B}'$ such that
460		\[
461			\bigl\| \phi_{\mathrm{A}} \ot \phi_{\mathrm{B}} \ket{\psi} - \ket{\mathrm{aux}} \ot \ket{\mathrm{EPR}_q}^{\ot M} \bigr\|^2 \leq \delta_{\mathrm{qld}}\;.
462		\]
463		% Transfer step added: the source (lines 1864--1875 of
464		% 14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex) passes directly from the
465		% conjugation estimates of lem:qld-unitary, which concern the
466		% unitarily conjugated operators V (M_h ot Id) V^dagger, to the
467		% corresponding estimates for the isometry phi, whose conjugation
468		% inserts the projection onto its range; the range-projection
469		% argument below supplies the missing step.
470		Item~2 of Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-unitary} concerns the unitarily conjugated operators $N^W_h = V_{\mathrm{A}} \, (M^{(\mathrm{Pauli},W)}_h)_{\mathrm{A}} \, V_{\mathrm{A}}^\dagger$, whereas conjugation by the isometry $\phi_{\mathrm{A}}$ additionally inserts the projection $Q_{\mathrm{A}} = \phi_{\mathrm{A}} \phi_{\mathrm{A}}^\dagger = V_{\mathrm{A}} \, \bigl(\ket{\mathrm{EPR}_q}\bra{\mathrm{EPR}_q}^{\ot M}\bigr)_{\mathrm{A}'\mathrm{A}''} \, V_{\mathrm{A}}^\dagger$ onto the range of $\phi_{\mathrm{A}}$: since $(M^{(\mathrm{Pauli},W)}_h)_{\mathrm{A}}$ and $\bigl(\ket{\mathrm{EPR}_q}\bra{\mathrm{EPR}_q}^{\ot M}\bigr)_{\mathrm{A}'\mathrm{A}''}$ act on disjoint registers and hence commute,
471		\[
472			\phi_{\mathrm{A}} \, (M^{(\mathrm{Pauli},W)}_h)_{\mathrm{A}} \, \phi_{\mathrm{A}}^\dagger
473			= V_{\mathrm{A}} \, \Bigl( (M^{(\mathrm{Pauli},W)}_h)_{\mathrm{A}} \ot \bigl(\ket{\mathrm{EPR}_q}\bra{\mathrm{EPR}_q}^{\ot M}\bigr)_{\mathrm{A}'\mathrm{A}''} \Bigr) \, V_{\mathrm{A}}^\dagger
474			= N^W_h \, Q_{\mathrm{A}} = Q_{\mathrm{A}} \, N^W_h\;.
