137			Using Naimark dilation (Theorem~\ref{thm:naimark}), each dilated
138			sub-measurement being completed to a projective measurement by assigning
139			to one fixed outcome the residual projector of its family, we may replace
140			$\mathcal S'$ by a projective strategy of exactly the same value.  Write
141			its state as $\ket{\psi'} \in \C^d_{A'} \ot \C^d_{B'}$.  Let
142			\[
143				\ket{\psi} = \frac{1}{\sqrt 2}\, \bigl( \ket{0}_{A}\ket{1}_{B}\ket{\psi'}_{A'B'} + \ket{1}_{A}\ket{0}_{B}\ket{\psi'_\tau}_{A'B'} \bigr) \in \bigl(\C^2_{A} \ot \C^d_{A'}\bigr) \ot \bigl(\C^2_{B} \ot \C^d_{B'}\bigr)\,,
